[[:db/retract 17592186204623 :question/answer-fields 17592186203626] [:db/retract 17592186204239 :question/answer-fields 17592186200122] [:db/retract 17592186204239 :question/answer-fields 17592186200133] [:db/retract 17592186204239 :question/answer-fields 17592186200127] {:db/id 17592186203899 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-579647d8-78b0-511b-8a94-882ec6fc1b22" "question-a8c98d98-74bc-5116-9f06-75c38fdcf981"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203695 :question/problem "Consider the following set:\n\n$$\nA = \\big\\{\\mathbb{R}_0^+, \\mathbb{R}_0^-, \\mathbb{R}\\big\\}\n$$\n\nGiven the relation $R$ on $A$ defined by\n\n$$\nX\\:R\\: Y \\quad \\Leftrightarrow \\quad X\\supset Y,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\mathbb{R} \\: R\\: \\mathbb{R}_0^-$\n\n- $\\mathbb{R}_0^- \\: R\\: \\mathbb{R}_0^+$\n\n- $\\mathbb{R}_0^+ \\: \\cancel{\\!R\\!} \\: \\mathbb{R}$" :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A = A^2.$\n\n$$\nR\\subseteq A^2\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x \\: R \\: y$ if and only if $(x,y) \\in R$\n\n- $x \\: \\require{cancel}\\cancel{\\!R\\!} \\: y$ if and only if $(x,y) \\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $X \\: R \\: Y$ if and only if $X\\supset Y.$ For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $\\supset$ are interchangeable, and\n\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\!R\\!}$ and $\\not\\supset$ are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $\\supset,$ we have $\\mathbb{R} \\supset \\mathbb{R}_0^-.$ This is equivalent to $\\mathbb{R}_0^- \\subset \\mathbb{R},$ which is true.\n\n- Statement II is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $\\supset,$ we have $\\mathbb{R}_0^- \\supset \\mathbb{R}_0^+.$ This is equivalent to $\\mathbb{R}_0^+ \\subset \\mathbb{R}_0^-,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement III is true. Replacing $\\cancel{\\!R\\!}$ with the symbol $\\not\\supset,$ we have $\\mathbb{R}_0^+ \\not\\supset \\mathbb{R}.$ This is equivalent to $\\mathbb{R} \\not\\subset \\mathbb{R}_0^+,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203900 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b5b2a52b-fd77-5422-b1dc-3a9ca690060e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203683 :question/problem "Consider the following set:\n\n$$\nA = \\big\\{\\mathbb{Z}, \\mathbb{Q}, \\mathbb{R}\\big\\}\n$$\n\nGiven the relation $R$ on $A$ defined by\n\n$$\nX\\:R\\: Y \\quad \\Leftrightarrow \\quad \\mathbb{Q} \\subseteq X \\cap Y,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\mathbb{Z} \\: R \\: \\mathbb{Q}$\n\n- $\\mathbb{R} \\: R \\: \\mathbb{R}$\n\n- $\\mathbb{Q} \\: \\cancel{\\!R\\!}\\: \\mathbb{R}$" :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A = A^2.$\n\n$$\nR\\subseteq A^2\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x \\: R \\: y$ if and only if $(x,y) \\in R$\n\n- $x \\: \\require{cancel}\\cancel{\\!R\\!} \\: y$ if and only if $(x,y) \\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $X \\: R \\: Y$ if and only if $\\mathbb{Q} \\subseteq X \\cap Y.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. In this case, we have $\\mathbb{Q} \\subseteq \\mathbb{Z} \\cap \\mathbb{Q},$ which is false.\n\n- Statement II is true. In this case, we have $\\mathbb{Q} \\subseteq \\mathbb{R} \\cap \\mathbb{R},$ which is true.\n\n- Statement III is false. In this case, we have $\\mathbb{Q} \\not\\subseteq \\mathbb{Q} \\cap \\mathbb{R},$ which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203901 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e2674a53-8856-5a0e-8ea3-7bef241518ca"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203691 :question/problem "Let $A = \\mathbb{R},$ and consider the relation $R$ on $A$ such that $x \\: R \\: y$ if and only if $x$ and $y$ both lie above the upward-opening parabola whose focus is at $\\left(0,\\dfrac14\\right)$ and whose vertex is at $O.$ Express $R$ using set-builder notation." :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A = A^2.$\n\n$$\nR\\subseteq A\\times A\n$$\n\nFor a relation $R$ on a set $A,$ we also have the following notations:\n\n- $a \\: R \\: b$ if and only if $(a,b) \\in R$\n\n- $a \\: \\cancel{\\!R\\!} \\: b$ if and only if $(a,b) \\notin R$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y) \\in \\mathbb{R} \\times \\mathbb{R} = \\mathbb{R}^2$ such that $y \\gt x^2.$\n\n![](images/26/26671c4dc03b13afc43172e486602bf3d647f8be911769c24a9e0523f591b64b.png)\n\nTherefore, we can write out $R$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nR = \\Big\\{ (x,y) \\in \\mathbb{R}^2 \\: : \\: y \\gt x^2 \\Big\\}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-579647d8-78b0-511b-8a94-882ec6fc1b22" :question/id #uuid "579647d8-78b0-511b-8a94-882ec6fc1b22" :question/math-academy-id "q-212923" :question/problem "Given the relation $R$ on $N$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x>y,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $6\\,R\\,8$\n- $7\\,R\\,2$\n- $9\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,1$" :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x>y.$ For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $>$ are interchangeable, and\n\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $≯$ (or, equivalently, $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $\\le $) are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $>,$ we have $6>8,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement II is true. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $>,$ we have $7>2,$ which is true.\n\n- Statement III is false. Replacing $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ with the symbol $\\le ,$ we have $9\\le 1,$ which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2932e32f-ef14-5573-93fb-85f8c4797761"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2932e32f-ef14-5573-93fb-85f8c4797761" :answer-field/id #uuid "2932e32f-ef14-5573-93fb-85f8c4797761" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-08f7679f-73f5-5a0e-a03f-dee0f63f3f77" :answer-field/choices ["answer-73e34a12-d804-5c4c-b0b0-abf70c77b752" "answer-2ddca7f1-da8d-5b3b-a8af-f028a712c9a2" "answer-3e90ef8b-8d7b-59de-9f36-95572e6e5a15" "answer-08f7679f-73f5-5a0e-a03f-dee0f63f3f77" "answer-47f66e07-d1c0-5f79-82e3-fcb796015fd1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73e34a12-d804-5c4c-b0b0-abf70c77b752" :answer/id #uuid "73e34a12-d804-5c4c-b0b0-abf70c77b752" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ddca7f1-da8d-5b3b-a8af-f028a712c9a2" :answer/id #uuid "2ddca7f1-da8d-5b3b-a8af-f028a712c9a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e90ef8b-8d7b-59de-9f36-95572e6e5a15" :answer/id #uuid "3e90ef8b-8d7b-59de-9f36-95572e6e5a15" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08f7679f-73f5-5a0e-a03f-dee0f63f3f77" :answer/id #uuid "08f7679f-73f5-5a0e-a03f-dee0f63f3f77" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47f66e07-d1c0-5f79-82e3-fcb796015fd1" :answer/id #uuid "47f66e07-d1c0-5f79-82e3-fcb796015fd1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a8c98d98-74bc-5116-9f06-75c38fdcf981" :question/id #uuid "a8c98d98-74bc-5116-9f06-75c38fdcf981" :question/math-academy-id "q-212926" :question/problem "Given the relation $R$ on $Z$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x∣y,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $6\\,R\\,3$\n- $5\\,R\\,8$\n- $7\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,9$" :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x∣y.$ For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $∣$ are interchangeable, and\n\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $∤$ are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $∣,$ we have $6∣3,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement II is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $∣,$ we have $5∣8,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement III is true. Replacing $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ with the symbol $∤,$ we have $7∤9,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-48ac91af-23e6-5125-89c4-136992dc2060"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-48ac91af-23e6-5125-89c4-136992dc2060" :answer-field/id #uuid "48ac91af-23e6-5125-89c4-136992dc2060" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f4fc5035-39d1-5b29-9501-8255ecdfee6a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cfb80eb9-1870-59ae-9a1d-0cda06ea7804" "answer-d24a8b3d-e9ae-577a-92d3-05c2bbc465f8" "answer-4de08473-7aaa-5afc-bd97-107dd067e857" "answer-1f17869c-0ece-5ef7-a77d-d4d3abc9fe0f" "answer-f4fc5035-39d1-5b29-9501-8255ecdfee6a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cfb80eb9-1870-59ae-9a1d-0cda06ea7804" :answer/id #uuid "cfb80eb9-1870-59ae-9a1d-0cda06ea7804" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d24a8b3d-e9ae-577a-92d3-05c2bbc465f8" :answer/id #uuid "d24a8b3d-e9ae-577a-92d3-05c2bbc465f8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4de08473-7aaa-5afc-bd97-107dd067e857" :answer/id #uuid "4de08473-7aaa-5afc-bd97-107dd067e857" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f17869c-0ece-5ef7-a77d-d4d3abc9fe0f" :answer/id #uuid "1f17869c-0ece-5ef7-a77d-d4d3abc9fe0f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4fc5035-39d1-5b29-9501-8255ecdfee6a" :answer/id #uuid "f4fc5035-39d1-5b29-9501-8255ecdfee6a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204623 :question/problem "Given the relation $R$ on $Z$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x∣(y-1),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $4\\,R\\,13$\n- $3\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,11$\n- $8\\,R\\,3$" :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x∣(y-1).$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. In this case, we have $4∣(13-1),$ which is true.\n\n- Statement II is true. In this case, we have $3∤(11-1),$ which is true.\n\n- Statement III is false. In this case, we have $8∣(3-1),$ which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-856a64a3-53df-597c-9cc5-75ee45f124c8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-856a64a3-53df-597c-9cc5-75ee45f124c8" :answer-field/id #uuid "856a64a3-53df-597c-9cc5-75ee45f124c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-24ec285a-89b6-5e80-85cf-547592c0be93" :answer-field/choices ["answer-24ec285a-89b6-5e80-85cf-547592c0be93" "answer-4a6224af-2752-5783-be20-5ad5862f62d9" "answer-516f8b78-7d59-5ec9-ba7c-04b73f06ad86" "answer-29192154-5fca-5c4c-ba05-c1677c12f786" "answer-85e2f0d3-5246-5ae6-9a99-5800a2b254f6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24ec285a-89b6-5e80-85cf-547592c0be93" :answer/id #uuid "24ec285a-89b6-5e80-85cf-547592c0be93" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a6224af-2752-5783-be20-5ad5862f62d9" :answer/id #uuid "4a6224af-2752-5783-be20-5ad5862f62d9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-516f8b78-7d59-5ec9-ba7c-04b73f06ad86" :answer/id #uuid "516f8b78-7d59-5ec9-ba7c-04b73f06ad86" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29192154-5fca-5c4c-ba05-c1677c12f786" :answer/id #uuid "29192154-5fca-5c4c-ba05-c1677c12f786" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85e2f0d3-5246-5ae6-9a99-5800a2b254f6" :answer/id #uuid "85e2f0d3-5246-5ae6-9a99-5800a2b254f6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b5b2a52b-fd77-5422-b1dc-3a9ca690060e" :question/id #uuid "b5b2a52b-fd77-5422-b1dc-3a9ca690060e" :question/math-academy-id "q-212983" :question/problem "Given the relation $R$ on $Z$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x≡y+4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $0\\,R\\,2$\n- $1\\,R\\,9$\n- $4\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,13$" :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x≡y+4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6),$ or equivalently, $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $6∣(x-y-4).$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. In this case, we have $6∣(0-2-4),$ which is true.\n\n- Statement II is true. In this case, we have $6∣(1-9-4),$ which is true.\n\n- Statement III is true. In this case, we have $6∤(4-13-4),$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7d5bc513-fdb3-5851-90bf-ada4837ec06e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7d5bc513-fdb3-5851-90bf-ada4837ec06e" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d5bc513-fdb3-5851-90bf-ada4837ec06e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9f73524d-1b4f-5845-812e-02bb16d1c56e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-665cfac7-9e55-5543-a679-b699d85f4d54" "answer-9f73524d-1b4f-5845-812e-02bb16d1c56e" "answer-eb20f44b-f74b-58f6-88d3-202204570fca" "answer-5b8dfe07-93a1-57b4-9823-f9fcd6b4b485" "answer-52d27a60-60f5-5754-a7bb-f26a821748ee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-665cfac7-9e55-5543-a679-b699d85f4d54" :answer/id #uuid "665cfac7-9e55-5543-a679-b699d85f4d54" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f73524d-1b4f-5845-812e-02bb16d1c56e" :answer/id #uuid "9f73524d-1b4f-5845-812e-02bb16d1c56e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb20f44b-f74b-58f6-88d3-202204570fca" :answer/id #uuid "eb20f44b-f74b-58f6-88d3-202204570fca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b8dfe07-93a1-57b4-9823-f9fcd6b4b485" :answer/id #uuid "5b8dfe07-93a1-57b4-9823-f9fcd6b4b485" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52d27a60-60f5-5754-a7bb-f26a821748ee" :answer/id #uuid "52d27a60-60f5-5754-a7bb-f26a821748ee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204239 :question/problem "Let $A=R,$ and consider the relation \"greater than or equal to\" on $A.$ Express the relation using set-builder notation." :question/worked-solution "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nFor a relation $R$ on a set $A,$ we also have the following notations:\n\n- $a\\,R\\,b$ if and only if $(a,b)\\in R$\n\n- $a\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,b$ if and only if $(a,b)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}$ such that $x\\ge y.$\n\nTherefore, we can write out $R$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ge y}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7d1c0b7d-5f9f-5a16-ba5e-5fbaabb0ff87" "answer-field-0cfc3d7a-2259-57ab-ba49-9efd8b42e165" "answer-field-a96a19a5-4d57-5c70-b981-f077301f5ca5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7d1c0b7d-5f9f-5a16-ba5e-5fbaabb0ff87" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d1c0b7d-5f9f-5a16-ba5e-5fbaabb0ff87" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-1b24f77e-0b5e-5992-aab2-7c2712cb6787" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dfac508c-e485-5a32-a413-ba05ce3e812c" "answer-1b24f77e-0b5e-5992-aab2-7c2712cb6787" "answer-b7c29e5e-005d-5aa4-a308-8de717ca5124" "answer-ecf05330-5148-5979-80aa-4753107e88c5" "answer-875da723-a73e-5e99-abfd-438df48efd55"] :db/ensure 